From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhugengyu <zhugengyu2023@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Nov 2026 19:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wifi: rtl8xxxu: set the station macid in the v3 TX descriptor

rtl8xxxu_fill_txdesc_v3() receives the frame's macid and never writes it
into the descriptor, so every frame is sent as macid 0.  In STA mode that
is the broadcast macid and matches the status quo, but an AP must send a
station's unicast frames and management responses with that station's
macid: the firmware keys its per-station state (rate, ACK/BA, TIM) on
it.  This is the gap the rtl8xxxu maintainer named in review of the
8188EU AP-mode RFC:
  https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2603.1/12855.html

The vendor 8188EU driver writes mac_id & 0x3F into the low bits of txdw1
for both data and management frames (hal/rtl8188eu_xmit.c:228,288); the
queue lives at [12:8] and nothing else uses [5:0], so the field is safe
to take.  The define is the 32-byte-descriptor counterpart of the
existing TXDESC40_MACID_* pair.

Signed-off-by: zhugengyu <zhugengyu2023@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/core.c b/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/core.c
index bddbd09..1fa2dc6 100644
--- a/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/core.c
+++ b/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/core.c
@@ -5391,6 +5391,14 @@ rtl8xxxu_fill_txdesc_v3(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr,
 
 	seq_number = IEEE80211_SEQ_TO_SN(le16_to_cpu(hdr->seq_ctrl));
 
+	/* The descriptor's low six bits of txdw1 are the frame's macid on the
+	 * v3 chips (queue at [12:8]); the firmware keys its per-station state
+	 * on it, so an AP's unicast frames and management responses must carry
+	 * the station's macid, not 0.  The vendor driver writes mac_id & 0x3F
+	 * here for both data and management frames (hal/rtl8188eu_xmit.c:228,
+	 * 288); STA mode is unchanged because its macids are 0/1. */
+	tx_desc->txdw1 |= cpu_to_le32(macid & TXDESC32_MACID_MASK);
+
 	if (ieee80211_is_data(hdr->frame_control)) {
 		rate = ra->decision_rate;
 		tx_desc->txdw5 = cpu_to_le32(rate);
diff --git a/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/rtl8xxxu.h b/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/rtl8xxxu.h
index eeb18eb..dbcac6c 100644
--- a/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/rtl8xxxu.h
+++ b/wireless-drivers/rtl8xxxu/rtl8xxxu.h
@@ -491,6 +491,9 @@ struct rtl8xxxu_txdesc40 {
 #define TXDESC32_AGG_BREAK		BIT(6)
 #define TXDESC40_MACID_SHIFT		0
 #define TXDESC40_MACID_MASK		0x00f0
+/* 32-byte descriptor (the v3 tx path): bits 0-5 of txdw1 carry the macid,
+ * the queue is at [12:8] (vendor hal/rtl8188eu_xmit.c: mac_id & 0x3F). */
+#define TXDESC32_MACID_MASK		0x3f
 #define TXDESC_QUEUE_SHIFT		8
 #define TXDESC_QUEUE_MASK		0x1f00
 #define TXDESC_QUEUE_BK			0x2
